  "evidence": "TEXT_E: Brexit implementation (leave EU law, single market, customs union); strong policing and justice measures (20,000 extra police, tougher sentences, end automatic halfway release); defence commitments (exceed NATO 2%, maintain nuclear deterrent, Space Command); immigration control (Australian-style points system, stronger enforcement, English language integration); union emphasis and veterans’ support; voter ID safeguards. Also NHS funding uplift and social care guarantees. TEXT_G: Independence referendum for Scotland; closest possible EU relationship and support for a second EU referendum; cancel the UK nuclear weapons system; supervised drug consumption facilities and treating drug deaths as a public health issue; devolved/lenient immigration (Scottish Visa, end indefinite detention, expand family reunion, allow asylum seekers to work); extensive welfare expansions and rights protections; replace FPTP with STV and extend the franchise.",
  "reasoning": "Given the electorate’s high weighting for Authority and Loyalty, TEXT_E’s emphasis on law‑and‑order, defence and nuclear deterrence, border control, voter ID, and preserving national institutions better matches those priorities while still offering some care and proportionality provisions. TEXT_G prioritizes equality and care but weakens Authority/Loyalty signals through independence moves, anti‑nuclear stance, and more permissive justice/immigration policies, making it a poorer fit for the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
